The class linker logs each class, method and field it fails to resolve (the Unity test APK probe, minato_resolve_log.h).

An app that catches a NoClassDefFoundError names no gap: Unity's activity died on a missing android.app.Dialog, and
the run showed only a later NoSuchFieldError. Where DoResolveType turns a ClassNotFoundException into a
NoClassDefFoundError, and where ResolveMethod, ResolveField and ResolveFieldJLS throw NoSuchMethodError and
NoSuchFieldError, a warning with the tag minato-resolve names what is missing and the method that asks, once; the
verifier names the method it verifies for the resolutions it makes. A boot class that names a class the boot class
path lacks, and JNI's FindClass on a thread whose code has no loader, get FindClass's pre-allocated
NoClassDefFoundError, without the name or a stack; FindClass names a platform class it lacks there, any other class
only by its library family, and who asks: the method verified, or else the thread's Java frames, masked the same way.
Thread's SetException names who sets that error outside the boot branch (a rethrow, as Class.forName makes of a
ClassNotFoundException's cause), and HandleUncaughtExceptions, for an uncaught one, the thread's last miss and throw.

